# Cloudflare Pages response headers — security baseline for the public-body site.
# adapter-cloudflare copies this root _headers file verbatim into .svelte-kit/cloudflare.
#
# NOTE: Content-Security-Policy is NOT set here. SvelteKit's hydration bootstrap
# is an inline <script> whose sha256 hash changes every build, so a static
# header policy with script-src 'self' would block it (it did — broke the mobile
# nav drawer). The CSP is managed by kit.csp in svelte.config.js (hash/nonce
# mode). Framing protection stays here via X-Frame-Options: DENY, because
# frame-ancestors is ignored in <meta>-delivered CSP.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=()

# Path-scoped CSP for the self-hosted Sveltia editor. This governs /admin (static
# HTML outside SvelteKit); the prerendered site pages keep their own CSP in
# svelte.config.js (kit.csp) which is NOT touched here (Pitfall 3). The Sveltia SPA
# is served from a pinned local bundle (script-src 'self'); it talks only to the
# GitHub API and to the OAuth proxy Worker, and opens the GitHub login in a popup.
# TODO(Plan 05): the workers.dev origin below is a placeholder that MUST match
# config.yml `base_url`; finalize both to the deployed sveltia-cms-auth Worker.
/admin/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://avatars.githubusercontent.com https://raw.githubusercontent.com; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://api.github.com https://sveltia-cms-auth.zlobekstromiec.workers.dev; frame-src https://github.com; form-action 'self' https://github.com; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'
